{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c12dce2d-6cd5-4954-8940-481169a85e10","step":{"id":"s1","script":"An angle at the center cuts off an arc. We measure the arc length along the circle, not straight across it.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"C1","content":"Radians measure arc length"},{"op":"figure","id":"circlefig","region":"left","frame":{"x":[-2.6,2.8],"y":[-2.5,2.7],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"circle","id":"circle","center":[0,0],"r":2},{"kind":"point","id":"center","at":[0,0],"label":"O"},{"kind":"point","id":"start","at":[2,0]},{"kind":"segment","id":"radius","from":{"at":"center"},"to":{"at":"start"},"label":"r"},{"kind":"arc","id":"arc","center":{"at":"center"},"r":2,"start":0,"end":60,"label":"s"},{"kind":"point","id":"end","at":{"on":"arc","t":1}}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c12dce2d-6cd5-4954-8940-481169a85e10","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The angle in radians is arc length divided by radius. One radian cuts off an arc exactly as long as the radius.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"anglemarks","on":"circlefig","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"center"},"to":{"at":"end"}},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"center"},"from":{"at":"start"},"to":{"at":"end"},"r":0.18,"label":"θ"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"definition","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\theta=\\frac{s}{r}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad s=r\\theta"},{"op":"equation","id":"oneradian","anchor":{"el":"definition","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"s=r\\ \\Longrightarrow\\ \\theta=1\\text{ rad}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"c12dce2d-6cd5-4954-8940-481169a85e10","step":{"id":"s3","script":"For this sixty-degree angle, use pi over three radians. With radius two meters, the arc length is two pi over three meters.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"values","on":"circlefig","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[1,-0.3],"text":"2 m"},{"kind":"text","at":[0.85,0.55],"text":"60°"},{"kind":"text","at":[2.05,1.6],"text":"2π/3 m","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"conversion","anchor":{"el":"oneradian","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"60^\\circ=\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\text{ rad}"},{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"conversion","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"s=2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\text{ m}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
